<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Seir Kieran</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Saighir</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Seir Kieran, in Irish Saighir, is a site in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-offaly">County Offaly</a>, Ireland, where Saint <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ciaran-of-saighir">Ciarán the Elder</a> founded one of Ireland's earliest monasteries in the 5th or 6th century. It was the chief church of Osraige and a burial place of its kings, until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aghaboe">Aghaboe</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kilkenny">Kilkenny</a> overtook it. Remains of a round tower base, a high cross and early graveslabs survive.</p></div>
